\]
and $g_0(t)$ runs over smooth functions supported on $t \asymp 1$, satisfying $||g_0^{(j)}||_\infty \ll_j 1$ for each $j \ge 0$ (with fixed implicit constants). Here $\mu = \mu(\ell_1, \ell_2, t, e_0, e_1', e_2', d)$ is the unique solution $\pmod{te_0e_1'e_2'}$ to the congruences $\mu \equiv d\overline{\ell_1} \pmod{te_0e_1'}$ and $\mu \equiv d\overline{\ell_2} \pmod{te_0e_2'}$.

\[
\begin{aligned}
